{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Unto the elders of Midian.</b> Now were they not from of old haters one of the other, as it says ״הַמַּכֶּה אֶת מִדְיָן בִּשְׂדֵה מוֹאָב״ (Genesis 36) — that Midian came against Moab to battle? Rather, out of their fear of Israel they made peace between themselves. And what did Moab see to take counsel from Midian? Since they saw Israel prevailing not according to the way of the world, they said: their leader was raised in Midian — let us ask them what his nature is. They said to them: his power is only in his mouth. They said: we too will come against them with a man whose power is in his mouth (Tanchuma)." "<b>As the ox licks.</b> All that the ox licks has no blessing in it (ibid.)." "<b>At that time.</b> He was not fit for kingship — he was of the princes of Midian; and once Sihon died, they appointed him over them for the need of the hour (ibid.)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:08.947242642Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}